Build the New Relic CLI for GOOS=wasip1.

Reason: newrelic v0.117.0 builds for wasip1 except for four packages.
github.com/sirupsen/logrus v1.9.3 builds terminal_check_notappengine.go
(which calls isTerminal) for wasip1 but has no wasip1 isTerminal; wasip1
now takes its js/nacl/plan9 file, which answers "not a terminal".
github.com/AlecAivazis/survey/v2/terminal's runereader_posix.go sets raw
mode with termios ioctls, which wasip1 doesn't have; wasip1 gets a file
without them. A survey prompt can't work without raw mode: on
slicc-kernel's terminal it asks for the cursor position, the cooked
terminal holds the answer until Enter, and the prompt hangs. So on wasip1
survey.Ask refuses before any I/O with "cannot prompt: WASI preview1 has
no terminal raw mode; pass the value as a flag" (newrelic profile add
then needs every value as a flag, or -y). mvdan.cc/sh/v3/interp's
os_unix.go uses unix.Mkfifo and Stat_t owners; wasip1 gets windows' answers (no mkfifo, directories
searchable). internal/install/validation has the integration directories
for linux, darwin and windows only; wasip1 takes darwin's /dev/null.
newrelic install, the only user of sh/interp and the validation, is
refused on wasip1 (0003).

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: logrus, survey, sh and newrelic-cli build for GOOS=wasip1
without it.

